  "name": "ANTI INSULIN ANTIBODIES",
  "code": "AIAB",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Test</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Normal Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Positive Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Anti-Insulin Antibodies (IAA)</strong></td>\n<td>Negative (No detectable antibodies)</td>\n<td>Detectable antibodies against insulin</td>\n<td>- <strong>Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (T1DM):</strong> Common in newly diagnosed children before insulin therapy; marker of autoimmune &beta;-cell destruction. - <strong>Insulin-treated patients:</strong> May develop antibodies to exogenous insulin &rarr; can cause insulin resistance, altered glucose control, or allergic reactions. - Rarely seen in other autoimmune disorders without diabetes.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul data-start=\"785\" data-end=\"1291\">\n<li data-start=\"785\" data-end=\"899\">\n<p data-start=\"787\" data-end=\"899\"><strong data-start=\"787\" data-end=\"834\">In newly diagnosed, insulin-na&iuml;ve patients:</strong> Positive IAA strongly suggests <strong data-start=\"866\" data-end=\"896\">autoimmune Type 1 Diabetes</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"900\" data-end=\"1049\">\n<p data-start=\"902\" data-end=\"1049\"><strong data-start=\"902\" data-end=\"945\">In patients already on insulin therapy:</strong> Presence of antibodies usually reflects immune response to injected insulin (not diagnostic of T1DM).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1190\">\n<p data-start=\"1052\" data-end=\"1190\">Usually interpreted <strong data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1116\">along with other diabetes autoantibodies</strong> (GAD65, IA-2, ZnT8, ICA) for accurate diagnosis of autoimmune diabetes.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1191\" data-end=\"1291\">\n<p data-start=\"1193\" data-end=\"1291\"><strong data-start=\"1193\" data-end=\"1209\">Negative IAA</strong> does not exclude Type 1 diabetes, since not all patients develop this antibody.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
